://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T12:05:30Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T13:00:32Z","body":"Updated the PR description. Latest version re-applies transform properties when the type (2d, 3d, control) is the same, and has a few conversions and fallbacks when you change type: \r\n- `Node2D` to `Node2D`: sets full transform.\r\n- `Node2D` to `Control`: sets position, rotation, and scale (not skew).\r\n- `Node2D` to `Node3D`: no fallback.\r\n- `Control` to `Control`: sets full transform.\r\n- `Control` to `Node2D`: sets full transform.\r\n- `Control` to `Node3D`: no fallback.\r\n- `Node3D` to `Node3D`: sets full transform.\r\n- `Node3D` to `Node2D`: no fallback.\r\n- `Node3D` to `Control`: no fallback. (I don't think setting position makes any sense here.)\r\n\r\nOn top of all this, replacing a MissingNode with a replacement preserves all applicable properties.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4406262484/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4406611303","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godo